// Up to the _, it fits in an i64 mantissa. Then the next digit causes a loss of
// precision, which is not an immediate error, it would only be if this was an
// integer. But due to the .0 at the end, that is fine. And then the next digit
// just increments the exponent once more.
9223372036854775807_1_2.0

# output:
9223372036854775807e2
